A||||4||Matthew_Fiero||keys broke in door||||1||
Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||09-04-2001||06:46 PM||||while turning the key to unlock my fiero the key snapped in half leaving the end of the key in the lock, now ANYONE can get into my car!!<BR>how do i get this out without any stupid hassles?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-04-2001||07:23 PM||||you may be able to get it out with a lock pic. If not prob have to take out lock cyl, which means inside door panel. If you do that, you may as well just replace it if it dont come out very easy. Other option is take it to a locksmith and see if they can retrieve it for you, save you a service call to come to you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||09-05-2001||11:27 PM||||If you do decide to take out the lock cylinder it's fairly easy to do. I just did this the other day and found I didn't even have to take the whole inner door panel off. Just loosened it enough to take the window trim off to get at the mirror bolts. The mirror has to come off to egt the door skin off. Once the door skin is off just pull the clip holding the lock in place put your new lock cylinder in and put everything back together. Ogres cave has a good article on pulling the door skins.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg"> <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project||||reg||1
Z||000003||sloth85GT||09-06-2001||01:45 AM||||I think a bat will solve your problems hehehehe But then again, that's my solution to all of lifes problems and computer problems, use a bat!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||09-06-2001||06:46 AM||||Get 2 pieces of thin, but durable wire about 4-5 inches long.  Put a little dab of high strength super glue on the tip of them.  Very carefully insert them into the lock cylinder and stick them to the back of the broken key.  Let it sit for a minute or two and them slowly pull the key out.  If you're not too careful you'll end up getting glued to the cylinder though, then you'll either need to remove it or call a locksmith.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
